            "detailed_description": "Zeran's Folly is a story-driven action-adventure with fluid melee combat, four unique playable characters, and a twisted sense of humor. Follow the adventures of Lone as he scours the land for the artifacts that will do... something. In the end, Lone will have to choose between abandoning either his friends or everything he's worked for. What would you choose?<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Content Warning</h2>This game contains crude/suggestive dialogue and some nudity of both sexes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Cool Stuff</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Switch instantly between up to seven unique playable characters anywhere in the world, each with their own abilities<br></li><li> Each character has multiple talents that can change their abilities and playstyle<br></li><li> Mountains of rings to find and equip that have effects from increasing money drops to changing attacks<br></li><li> Look your best with piles of alternate outfits for each character<br></li><li> Seven huge dungeons to conquer<br></li><li> Restart a new game with all your stuff by reliving your memories (New Game +).<br></li><li> Never lose progress from dying--just revive at the last Whisper Stone save point.<br></li><li> Extend your survivability with your trusty Hip Flask, an upgradeable health potion.<br></li><li> Rich and touching story, although it's more like a bad touch<br></li><li> Absolutely stunning art that's a feast for the eyes and possibly genitals<br></li><li> Fully supports and provides extra gameplay features for gamepads/controllers<br></li><li> A catchy soundtrack that bounces from island beats to cool country to headbanging metal<br></li><li> Over ten hours of gameplay on average</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Other Stuff</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Made with SFML</li></ul>",
            "about_the_game": "Zeran's Folly is a story-driven action-adventure with fluid melee combat, four unique playable characters, and a twisted sense of humor. Follow the adventures of Lone as he scours the land for the artifacts that will do... something. In the end, Lone will have to choose between abandoning either his friends or everything he's worked for. What would you choose?<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Content Warning</h2>This game contains crude/suggestive dialogue and some nudity of both sexes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Cool Stuff</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Switch instantly between up to seven unique playable characters anywhere in the world, each with their own abilities<br></li><li> Each character has multiple talents that can change their abilities and playstyle<br></li><li> Mountains of rings to find and equip that have effects from increasing money drops to changing attacks<br></li><li> Look your best with piles of alternate outfits for each character<br></li><li> Seven huge dungeons to conquer<br></li><li> Restart a new game with all your stuff by reliving your memories (New Game +).<br></li><li> Never lose progress from dying--just revive at the last Whisper Stone save point.<br></li><li> Extend your survivability with your trusty Hip Flask, an upgradeable health potion.<br></li><li> Rich and touching story, although it's more like a bad touch<br></li><li> Absolutely stunning art that's a feast for the eyes and possibly genitals<br></li><li> Fully supports and provides extra gameplay features for gamepads/controllers<br></li><li> A catchy soundtrack that bounces from island beats to cool country to headbanging metal<br></li><li> Over ten hours of gameplay on average</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Other Stuff</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Made with SFML</li></ul>",
            "short_description": "You're not a bad guy just because you have murderers as friends and holy knights want to kill you, right? Lone is on a quest with his two big axes and three loyal friends to find the four artifacts he needs in a world he doesn't bother to understand.",
            "supported_languages": "Inglês",
            "reviews": {
                "query_summary": {
                    "num_reviews": 1,
                    "review_score": 6,
                    "review_score_desc": "Mostly Positive",
                    "total_positive": 39,
                    "total_negative": 16,
                    "total_reviews": 55
                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236276037",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198052154176",
                            "num_reviews": 6,
                            "playtime_forever": 336,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 336,
                            "last_played": 1790460757
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "All the right bones for a great game in all the wrong sockets. This game doesn't understand what TONE means, and has some majorly inappropriate content that is definitely not for a younger audience. The game play can't decide if it wants to be sonic or ikaruga, and I found the experience of playing the game frustrating and honestly, not fun. \r\n\r\nIt was as if the developers know that \"game design\" mean that you designed the game, rather than thinking about how to shape the play space, train skills, and allow the player to feel capable. There is no dance, it is all just chaotic face slapping that punishes everything always. There canot be a platform that doesn't have a spike pit within 10 units apparently. Add to this that the controls were quite buggy, ESPECIALLY when it comes to jumping off of surfaces. God help you if you need to jump on a slope. I had to weigh trying to get up some slopes against the remaining years I have left on the earth.\r\n\r\nLike I said, the bones are all there for a great game, but they are not in the right sockets. I see what the developers were trying to do, but ultimately, they didn't do it. I was rooting for this to be a great title, it was on my wishlist for literally years, but it turns out to be one of the most frustrating and unfun metroidvanias I have ever played.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1790461202,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1790461202,
                        "voted_up": false,
